WEBVTT

00:13:58.917 --> 00:14:01.526
and it's an outdoor version
of a chatty table.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:05.019
AG: I have to say, I don't think I'd want
to sit on one of those benches.

00:14:05.043 --> 00:14:06.511
I prefer not to be approached.

00:14:06.535 --> 00:14:09.496
DB: We should perhaps both try it
and compare notes.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.118
AG: These kinds of programs
aren't enough by themselves

00:14:12.142 --> 00:14:14.019
to transform an organizational culture.

00:14:14.043 --> 00:14:15.292
But they can open a door

00:14:15.316 --> 00:14:19.386
and send a signal that it's OK
to seek connection with your colleagues.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:23.016
Now, not everyone works on a team
that prioritizes connection.

00:14:23.040 --> 00:14:26.076
Sometimes we have to take matters
into our own hands.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.142
Luz Claudio: Colleagues, I think, here ...

00:14:28.166 --> 00:14:33.956
the culture is more like people
seem to want to be more separate,